THOUGHT: The iterator inner classes require a LongMap instance in their constructors, so field initialization must happen in the constructor after validation, not at declaration. I’ll revert the field declarations to their original form and instead initialize entries1/2, values1/2, keys1/2 at the end of the LongMap(int, float) constructor, ensuring they’re always non-null on successful construction while avoiding the invalid no-arg constructor calls.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '80s/.*/  private transient Entries entries1, entries2;/;81s/.*/  private transient Values values1, values2;/;82s/.*/  private transient Keys keys1, keys2;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/LongMap.java && sed -i '118i\ \ \ \ entries1 = new Entries(this);
    entries2 = new Entries(this);
    values1 = new Values(this);
    values2 = new Values(this);
    keys1 = new Keys(this);
    keys2 = new Keys(this);' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/LongMap.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "LongMap.java" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

